+### Compound Format
+
+Use `compound` to combine units, largest first, skipping zero parts.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h 30m"
+ms(1999, { compound: true })          // "1s"
+```
+
+> [!NOTE]
+> Units range from days down to seconds, so larger spans are expressed in days (`8d`) and leftover milliseconds are dropped. Values under one second give `"0s"`. If `long` is also `true`, `long` takes precedence.
+
